# L §6.1 same: each side may name a row, "same a.rent[2026-03] = b.rent_in[2026-03]"; "Facts about them from both sides
# are read together, and a fact on which they disagree for a day is a hole naming both rows (HOLE-SAME), never a silent
# pick". ana states 2 000.00 PLN, ben 2 100.00 PLN: a hole read from either side. b.rent_in[2026-04] is no side of a
# same line: ben's row (2 100.00 PLN).
=== options pin=bytes
=== joint.tally
model family
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
  use a = "ana.tally" sha256 "e42519b086605a071d9ecc73cede5a0d6c7a969e069b921d3607f5353dd04a6c"
  use b = "ben.tally" sha256 "0100e9a6e9d46e4f564190c5f45cf81d6966cbd6c5a95b32effabbaea4534b0d"
  same a.rent[2026-03] = b.rent_in[2026-03]

ask ra: a.rent[2026-03]
ask rb: b.rent_in[2026-03]
ask r4: b.rent_in[2026-04]
=== ana.tally
model ana
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input rent[m in months]: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  rent[2026-03] = 2 000.00 PLN "umowa najmu"
=== ben.tally
model ben
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-05
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31

source s "umowa"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
input rent_in[m in months]: money PLN

version v
  cite s
  governs 2026..
  known 2025-12-01
  rent_in[2026-03] = 2 100.00 PLN "umowa najmu"
  rent_in[2026-04] = 2 100.00 PLN "umowa najmu"
=== expect ra rb r4
ra: ?"a.rent[2026-03] and b.rent_in[2026-03] are one, but the value differs on 2026-03-01: 2 000.00 PLN (a.v:a.rent[2026-03]) and 2 100.00 PLN (b.v:b.rent_in[2026-03])" (a.rent[2026-03], b.rent_in[2026-03])
...
rb: ?"b.rent_in[2026-03] and a.rent[2026-03] are one, but the value differs ...
...
r4: 2 100.00 PLN
...
